udy</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>1999</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>MS22</fpage><lpage>MS31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10098556</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00005650-199903001-00003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morales</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliott</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Weech-Maldonado</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Spritzer</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hays</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differences in CAHPS adult survey reports and ratings by race and ethnicity: an analysis of the National CAHPS benchmarking data 1.0</article-title><source>Health Serv Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>617</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11482591</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Solomon</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hays</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaslavsky</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cleary</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychometric properties of a group-level Consumer Assessment of Health Plans Study (CAHPS) instrument</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>2005</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15626934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spranca</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanouse</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliott</sur